      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "7. Having regard to the rival submissions made by both the learned counsel and having gone through the material available on record, it appears that the allegations against the petitioners are under sections 272, 273, 336 and 420 of the IPC"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "638d3ffdb5844bc9aedf44bf4de16543_20",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "8. It is significant to note the Judgment of the Hon'ble Supreme Court in State of Maharashtra and Anr vs. Sayyed Hassan and Sayyed Subhan and Ors 1., wherein it is observed that when there is no specific bar in the special enactment, the t"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b4c047b4a66a434fa8d85a6ada8d3fce_21",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The Enforcement Directorate of the Police is the specialized agency created for the purpose of investigation certain offence as specified in their manual."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "caa8dc4f6af74263a21c158705f3b358_22",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The Chapter Crime Rule 36 Laws of DEB manual has specified the enactment which does not include the Special Act."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "40bcd88f388144f0bd2ff38cf7a2729b_23",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Section 94 of the Special Act provides the State Government to make rules."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "2dfb72f4defa4e878e3f50046eece810_24",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "It has not been reported before this Court that whether the State Government have ever framed the rule empowering the Enforcement Directorate to investigate into the offence under the Special Act."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a72c6ead1835491ab980dbd946eff035_25",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The law of land empowers the investigating agency to investigate an offence according to the procedure laid down in the law; deviation thereto must have deprived the valuable right of the accused."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b5a7623a1b51403e96de1f7e0d05d9e1_26",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "\n1 (2019) 18 SCC 145 SKS,J 9."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "136bbbf892934271b7bbdde702fd0ae7_27",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "In the present case, the police have launched the prosecution according to the provisions of Cr.P.C. for the offence punishable under Sections 272 and 273 of IPC."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "56a03a05588e472f82a908380a2dc7a2_28",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The Police cannot launch a prosecution or conduct investigation in respect of offence of food related laws."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b4dcb19686b6466a8e8eea7d965a4a3e_29",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "The main contention of the counsel for the petitioners is that after the enactment of Special Act, the provision under Sections 272 and 273 of IPC has impliedly repealed."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "165fb483785a45c287e522849426afc8_30",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Thus, the investigation conducted by the Investigating Officer other than the Food Safety Officer is illegal."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "55cb5e195a7d43908f3506f2e5360843_31",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "10. As per the decision of the Hon'ble Supreme Court in Sayyed Hassan and Sayyed Subhan and also by virtue of the principle under Section 26 of General Clauses Act, investigation by the Police is not illegal and the petitioners shall not pu"
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "98575461067342e89caef5d8624ed2fe_32",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "As such, to safeguard the protection of the public, the Police can investigate the case of food relating offences when there is no specific bar under the Act."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "4d5e37d7a3364b82a53f8ec4be7b8f81_33",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Therefore, the investigation done by the Investigating Officer cannot be said to be vitiated."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b45ee6eda8d146d981ed655b2cc2c997_35",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "PRE_RELIED"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "As per the decision of the Hon'ble Supreme Court in Mukesh Singh vs. State (Narcotic Branch of Delhi) 2, wherein it is observed that where informant officer himself is an investigator, that by itself cannot be said that 2 (2020) 10 SCC 120 "
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "a4dbe854615549deb8be9684f96984f8_36",
      "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
      "labels": [
        "RATIO"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "Therefore,\nthe said contention is also not tenable."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "b44d161fbce648c1a9727bfad7ebb663_37",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
        "RPC"
      ],
      "reasons": [
        "forbidden_section:decision",
        "forbidden_labels:RPC",
        "suspicious_label:rpc"
      ],
      "matched_phrases": [],
      "text_preview": "12. However, in the light of the aforesaid discussion, this Court does not find any merit in the criminal petition to quash the proceedings against the petitioners and the same is liable to be dismissed."
    },
    {
      "annotation_id": "d0dceece16f44bf5a5af2e80edad1935_39",
      "summary_section": "decision",
      "labels": [
